{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance","kind":"proposition","title":"Spin involutions on Frobenius algebras leave the LP-dual shadow price invariant: $\\sigma(c) = c \\Rightarrow y_0^*(\\sigma(\\beta)) = y_0^*(\\beta)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-spin-involution"],"cites":["references/kassel1995","references/murphy1992"],"tags":["lp-duality","spin-involution","isospin-invariance","frobenius-algebra","hopf-antipode","shadow-price","structural-theorem","generic-framework"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.SpinInvolutionLPDualInvariance","text":"spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(A, \\tau)</code> be a Frobenius algebra with spin involution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c \\in A</code> be <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma</code>-invariant. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma</code> be a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma</code>-stable set of central idempotents of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>. For any <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\in A</code>, the optimal dual variable <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">y_0^*</code> of the operator-selection LP</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\min_{x \\in A}\\; \\tau(c \\cdot x)\n  \\quad \\text{s.t.} \\quad\n  \\tau(\\beta^* \\beta \\cdot x) = n_{\\mathrm{target}}(\\beta), \\;\\;\n  \\tau(\\pi_\\lambda \\cdot x) \\geq 0 \\;\\; \\forall \\lambda \\in \\Sigma</code></pre>\n<p><em>satisfies</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  y_0^*\\bigl(\\sigma(\\beta)\\bigr) \\;=\\; y_0^*(\\beta).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spin-involution-lp-dual-invariance.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.23.6"}
